The operational lesson is to connect an individual execution with the policy that determines how often it runs. Our editorial recommendation is to preserve request identity across retries, examine both tool outcomes and model calls, and compare cost against accepted work. When changing review frequency or model choice, record the rollout boundary alongside quality and latency signals. A lower price per call can still increase total spend or reviewer burden if the workflow performs more calls or produces less useful findings.

Why it matters: Measure the cost and usefulness of the whole agent workflow, and annotate behavior changes so fleet trends can be traced back to individual executions.

