Source: Arize Phoenix · GitHub release — https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/releases/tag/arize-phoenix-v20.23.0
Published: 2026-10-16
Channel: github

Phoenix v20.23.0 adds server-log export over OTLP. Its release notes also fix the playground’s handling of Bedrock tool results by forwarding them directly as text, and add documentation for Atomic Agents tracing. The short announcement does not provide deployment configuration, delivery guarantees, or performance measurements. Our editorial recommendation is to verify that server logs arrive at the intended receiver and remain distinguishable from application traces. Test a Bedrock tool-result round trip separately; a server logging feature does not establish correct application-level tool behavior.

Why it matters: Check the observability server’s own log delivery alongside application traces, using a known event rather than assuming export implies receipt.

